n class=\"italic\"> &nbsp &nbsp <br /> Example: There aren't any pens. </span></span><br />", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With non-count nouns you use a singular verb.<br /><sn class=\"strong\"> some </span> =  a small amount <span class=\"italic\"> &nbsp &nbsp <br />Example: There is some coffee.<br /></span><span class=\"strong\">not any</span> </span> = zero <span class=\"italic\"> &nbsp &nbsp <br />Example: There isn't any coffee. </span><br /></span><br />", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Asking Someone to Hand You Something in a Polite Way", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use polite language to ask a person to hand you something at work. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ashley</span>: Could you please hand me the stapler? <br /> <span class=\"strong\">Bruce</span>: Here you are. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Use <span class=\"italic\">Could you please + action ... ? </span> <br /> Use a polite answer like <span class=\"italic\"> Here you are. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Amanda</span>:  Could you please give me the book? <br /> <span class=\"strong\">Bart</span>: Yes, here you are.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to check", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to look carefully", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Let's check the supplies.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le05ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear at work.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "binder", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a cover for paper", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There is some paper in my school binder.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le05ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "ta